# Session 9: 1805, one player, the Allies, with the shipped NWS.CFG's Tactical on.
# The battle files, NAPOLEON.EXE and the result read back (docs\won-source-study.md,
# section 3.2).
seed 1
pace 1

wait 4
key space
wait 4
key s
wait 2
key down
wait 1
key enter
wait 3
shot objective
key space
wait 1
shot main-menu

# End the first turn. Bernadotte attacks Alexander in Innsbruck; the odds are within
# 3:1, so WON.EXE writes BATTLE.$$$ and runs NAPOLEON.EXE, which shows NAPIC.EXE's
# title picture first. No keys are typed until the battle map is up.
key e y
wait 30
shot attack
wait 15
shot tactical-title
key space
wait 5
shot battle-map

# The Allies command. Unit 1 (Alexander) rests; the next unit's turn comes up.
key space
wait 3
shot rested
# F9: strategic retreat, with a 20% penalty. The game asks "RETREAT?"; Yes ends the
# battle, writes OUTCOME.&&& and returns to WON.EXE.
key f9
wait 5
shot retreat-ask
key y
wait 6
shot victorious
wait 6
shot losses
wait 10
shot retreat
key v
wait 3
shot retreated
repeat 16
key space
wait 2
end
shot next-turn
